    <bpmn:process id="W_W1166" name="W1166. Carrier Rate Management, Freight Audit &amp; Cost Optimization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly carrier rate review cycle; or significant rate change from carrier; or quarterly benchmarking
Frequency: Monthly rate review; quarterly benchmarking; annual contract renewal
Volume: ~20–30 active carriers and freight forwarders (within the ~30–40 contracted base); ~PHP 600–800M annual freight spend (per W1439/W1440)
Owner: Logistics Manager
Participants: Logistics Manager, Procurement, Finance, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W1166 — Carrier Rate Management, Freight Audit &amp; Cost Optimization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1166_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1166_Lane1" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1166_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1166_Lane3" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1166_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1166_Start5" name="Monthly carrier rate review cycle; or significant rate change from carrier; or quarterly…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1166_Task6" name="Rate Card Maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Rate Card Maintenance: Logistics Manager maintains carrier rate cards in ERP: per-km rate by vehicle type, per-CBM rate for inter-island, per-delivery rate for last-mile, accessorial charges (waiting time, redelivery, hazmat surcharge per W237); updates on rate change notification from carrier
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1166_Task7" name="Freight Invoice Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Freight Invoice Audit: System performs automated freight audit: matches carrier invoice to dispatch manifest × contracted rate card; flags discrepancies &gt; 5%; AP Clerk investigates and resolves per W244
Responsible (R): System / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1166_Task8" name="Monthly Cost Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly Cost Analysis: Logistics Manager compiles monthly freight cost report: total spend by carrier, cost-per-delivery by zone, cost-per-CBM by lane, cost-per-km by vehicle type; compares to budget per W489
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1166_Task9" name="Quarterly Rate Benchmarking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly Rate Benchmarking: Procurement and Logistics Manager benchmark carrier rates against Philippine market: (a) solicit spot rates from alternative carriers, (b) compare to DTI-referenced transport rates, (c) analyze rate trends per SCP-019; identify lanes where BuildRight is above market
Responsible (R): Procurement / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1166_Task10" name="Rate Negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Rate Negotiation: For lanes above market benchmark: Logistics Manager negotiates rate reduction with incumbent carrier; if unsuccessful, Procurement issues RFQ per W224 to alternative carriers; evaluation criteria: rate 40%, reliability 30%, coverage 20%, technology 10%
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per carrier</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1166_Task11" name="Annual Contract Renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual Contract Renewal: For top-10 carriers by spend: annual contract renewal per W688 with updated rate schedules, SLA targets per SCP-020, insurance requirements per W610, and penalty clauses for repeated SLA breaches
Responsible (R): Procurement / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per W688</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1166_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1166_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1166_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1166_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-178 (ensure fleet compliance &amp; freight-cost integrity.) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Logistics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
