    <bpmn:process id="W_W1373" name="W1373. 3PL Carrier Driver Accreditation, Vehicle Inspection &amp; Compliance Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New 3PL driver assigned to BuildRight routes by carrier; or annual driver re-accreditation cycle; or driver involved in delivery incident per W1372
Frequency: Ongoing as drivers rotate; estimated 50–80 new driver accreditations/year across all carriers; annual re-accreditation for all active drivers
Volume: ~150–200 active 3PL drivers handling BuildRight deliveries chain-wide
Owner: Logistics Manager (HQ)
Participants: Logistics Manager, Carrier Fleet Manager, Safety Officer, HR (training records)
Source: workflow W1373 — 3PL Carrier Driver Accreditation, Vehicle Inspection &amp; Compliance Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1373_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1373_Lane1" name="Carrier Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1373_Lane2" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1373_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1373_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1373_Start5" name="New 3PL driver assigned to BuildRight routes by carrier; or annual driver…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task6" name="3PL carrier notifies Logistics Manager of new driver assignment: submits…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: 3PL carrier notifies Logistics Manager of new driver assignment: submits driver&#x27;s (a) professional driver&#x27;s license (restriction code 3 for both 6-wheeler and 10-wheeler trucks — heavy vehicles above 4,500 kg GVW); (b) LTO (Land Transportation Office) driving record clearance; (c) NBI/Police clearance; (d) drug test result (per DOLE Department Order 89-09 for drivers of heavy vehicles); (e) basic literacy certification (read/write English or Filipino)
Responsible (R): Carrier Fleet Manager / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task7" name="Logistics Manager verifies driver credentials: (a) checks LTO license validity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Logistics Manager verifies driver credentials: (a) checks LTO license validity online; (b) verifies restriction codes match assigned vehicle type; (c) reviews NBI clearance; (d) confirms drug test is within 6 months; (e) checks driver&#x27;s age (minimum 21 years per Philippine trucking standards)
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/driver</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task8" name="Carrier conducts vehicle inspection and submits Vehicle Condition Report: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Carrier conducts vehicle inspection and submits Vehicle Condition Report: (a) vehicle registration (current LTO registration); (b) annual vehicle inspection result (LTO Motor Vehicle Inspection); (c) tire condition (minimum tread depth, no recapped tires on front axle); (d) brake system condition; (e) lights, reflectors, and warning devices; (f) cargo securing equipment (tie-down straps, chains, tarpaulins); (g) fire extinguisher (required for cargo vehicles per LTO); (h) for refrigerated trucks (if applicable): reefer unit temperature maintenance verification
Responsible (R): Carrier Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task9" name="If driver credentials and vehicle condition are satisfactory: Logistics Manager…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If driver credentials and vehicle condition are satisfactory: Logistics Manager activates driver in system: (a) creates driver accreditation record linked to carrier master; (b) assigns driver to eligible routes/zones; (c) issues BuildRight carrier driver ID badge with photo; (d) grants carrier app access for route plans, POD capture, and delivery confirmations
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/driver</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task10" name="Driver completes BuildRight delivery orientation (can be done by carrier with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Driver completes BuildRight delivery orientation (can be done by carrier with BuildRight-provided materials): (a) BuildRight store receiving protocol (check in with Store Receiving Clerk, wait for unloading, obtain POD signature); (b) cargo securing standards (tarpaulin for weather protection, strap tension requirements for tiles and lumber); (c) carrier app usage (route navigation, stop check-in, POD capture, incident reporting); (d) emergency procedures (accident, breakdown, cargo shift during transit); (e) prohibited behaviors (unauthorized stops, drinking, using phone while driving, soliciting tips from stores)
Responsible (R): Carrier Fleet Manager / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): Safety Officer
Duration: 2 hours/driver</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1373_Task11" name="System tracks driver performance: (a) on-time delivery rate per driver; (b) POD…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: System tracks driver performance: (a) on-time delivery rate per driver; (b) POD completion rate per driver; (c) delivery incident count (damage, shortage) per driver per W1372; (d) driver ratings from Store Receiving Clerks (optional feedback via handheld after each delivery); (e) drivers with &gt; 2 incidents in 30 days flagged for review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task12" name="Annual re-accreditation: (a) driver submits updated license, NBI clearance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual re-accreditation: (a) driver submits updated license, NBI clearance, drug test; (b) carrier submits updated Vehicle Condition Report; (c) Logistics Manager reviews 12-month driver performance; (d) drivers with satisfactory performance and clean records renewed; (e) drivers with persistent issues not renewed — carrier must assign replacement driver
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / Carrier Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min/driver</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1373_Task13" name="If driver involved in delivery incident per W1372: (a) Logistics Manager…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: If driver involved in delivery incident per W1372: (a) Logistics Manager reviews incident severity; (b) for minor incidents (first occurrence, minor damage): driver receives written warning and mandatory re-orientation per Step 5; (c) for major incidents (high-value damage, theft suspicion, safety violation): driver accreditation suspended pending investigation; carrier must assign replacement driver within 48 hours; (d) for confirmed theft or gross negligence: driver accreditation permanently revoked; carrier notified; incident reported to LTO if warranted
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1373_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1373_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
