    <bpmn:process id="W_W1439" name="W1439. Third-Party Logistics (3PL) Partner Quarterly Business Review, Rate Benchmarking &amp; Contract Optimization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly 3PL review cycle; or significant service level failure; or annual contract renewal
Frequency: Quarterly formal business review; monthly KPI monitoring; annual contract negotiation
Volume: 8–10 active 3PL partners handling ~80% of outbound deliveries; ~PHP 600–800M annual freight spend
Owner: Logistics Manager
Participants: Logistics Manager, VP Supply Chain, Finance Controller, 3PL Partner Account Manager, AP Clerk
Source: workflow W1439 — Third-Party Logistics (3PL) Partner Quarterly Business Review, Rate Benchmarking &amp; Contract Optimization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1439_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1439_Lane1" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1439_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1439_Lane3" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1439_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1439_Start5" name="Quarterly 3PL review cycle; or significant service level failure; or annual contract…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1439_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1439_Task6" name="Quarterly performance scorecard preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly performance scorecard preparation: Logistics Manager compiles 3PL scorecard for each partner: (a) on-time delivery rate (target: ≥ 95%), (b) delivery damage rate (target: &lt; 0.5%), (c) POD submission timeliness (target: &lt; 24 hours), (d) driver compliance incidents (license, vehicle condition per W1373), (e) invoice accuracy (match rate of freight invoices to agreed rates), (f) responsiveness to ad-hoc requests and surge capacity, (g) customer complaint rate (delivery-related)
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/partner</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1439_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1439_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1439_Task7" name="Rate benchmarking analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Rate benchmarking analysis: Finance Controller and Logistics Manager conduct rate benchmarking: (a) compare each 3PL&#x27;s actual rates per route against: (i) industry published rates (LTL, FTL benchmarks from Philippine trucking associations), (ii) competitive quotes from alternative carriers, (iii) internal cost estimates (own fleet cost per km), (b) identify routes where current 3PL rates exceed benchmark by &gt; 10%, (c) identify routes where 3PL rates are competitive and volume should be maintained or increased
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1439_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1439_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1439_Task8" name="Quarterly business review meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly business review meeting: Logistics Manager and VP Supply Chain conduct QBR with each 3PL partner: (a) present performance scorecard — celebrate strengths, address deficiencies with improvement timeline, (b) discuss rate adjustments: negotiate reductions on over-benchmark routes; agree on fuel surcharge formula if not already in contract, (c) capacity planning: confirm 3PL can support projected volume increase (10–15 new stores/year), (d) review service level agreement compliance and penalties, (e) document action items with deadlines
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours/partner</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1439_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1439_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1439_Task9" name="Contract optimization recommendations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Contract optimization recommendations: Based on QBR findings, Logistics Manager recommends: (a) volume consolidation — shift more lanes to best-performing, best-priced 3PL partners, (b) rate renegotiation — target 5–10% reduction on over-benchmark routes, (c) contract term adjustments — extend contracts for top performers (price stability), shorten or terminate underperformers, (d) new lane assignments — rebalance load across partners to prevent single-partner dependency, (e) present recommendations to COO for approval
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1439_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1439_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1439_Task10" name="Annual contract renewal negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual contract renewal negotiation: For contracts expiring within 90 days: (a) Logistics Manager prepares renewal proposal based on 4 quarters of QBR data, (b) negotiate multi-year rates with annual escalation caps (e.g., max 5% annual increase), (c) include performance-based incentives (bonus for &gt; 98% OTD) and penalties (credit for &lt; 90% OTD), (d) COO approves final contract terms, (e) Legal reviews contract language per standard procurement process
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 8–16 hours/partner</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1439_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1439_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1439_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1439_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1439_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-258 (ensure controlled execution — Last-Mile &amp; Delivery Partners (PA-06.3).) | - operational: Logistics Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Logistics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1439_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1439_Annotation12" targetRef="W1439_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
