    <bpmn:process id="W_W1440" name="W1440. Fuel Price Volatility Impact Assessment, Freight Cost Adjustment &amp; Route Efficiency Optimization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly Philippine fuel price adjustment (every Tuesday); or monthly freight cost review; or fuel price change &gt; PHP 3/liter in a single adjustment
Frequency: Weekly monitoring (fuel prices); monthly freight cost impact review; quarterly route optimization assessment
Volume: ~200 delivery routes across 4 DCs serving 200 stores; ~PHP 600–800M annual freight spend of which ~30–35% is fuel cost (~PHP 180–280M)
Owner: Logistics Manager
Participants: Logistics Manager, VP Supply Chain, Finance Controller, Route Planners, 3PL Partners
Source: workflow W1440 — Fuel Price Volatility Impact Assessment, Freight Cost Adjustment &amp; Route Efficiency Optimization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1440_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1440_Lane1" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1440_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1440_Lane3" name="Route Planners">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1440_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1440_Start5" name="Weekly Philippine fuel price adjustment (every Tuesday); or monthly freight cost review…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1440_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1440_Task6" name="Weekly fuel price monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly fuel price monitoring: Logistics Manager tracks weekly diesel price adjustments (DOE Philippines publishes every Tuesday): (a) current diesel price per liter by region (Luzon, Visayas, Mindanao prices differ due to shipping costs), (b) week-over-week change, (c) year-to-date average vs. budgeted fuel price for freight cost planning, (d) if fuel price change &gt; PHP 3/liter in a single week: trigger immediate impact assessment
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1440_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1440_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1440_Task7" name="Monthly freight cost impact assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly freight cost impact assessment: Finance Controller and Logistics Manager assess monthly fuel cost impact: (a) calculate actual fuel cost component of freight spend (from 3PL invoices and own fleet fuel receipts), (b) compare to budgeted fuel cost (freight budget assumes PHP X/liter diesel), (c) calculate variance: actual fuel cost vs. budget × volume, (d) if variance &gt; 5% of monthly freight budget: escalate to VP Supply Chain and CFO for freight budget adjustment or SRP impact review
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1440_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1440_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1440_Task8" name="3PL fuel surcharge verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: 3PL fuel surcharge verification: For 3PL partners with fuel surcharge clauses: (a) Logistics Manager verifies surcharge calculation against DOE published diesel prices, (b) validate surcharge formula matches contract terms (e.g., surcharge = (actual diesel price − base diesel price) × km × liters/km factor), (c) flag discrepancies where 3PL surcharge exceeds contractually agreed amount, (d) dispute incorrect surcharges through AP process per W7
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1440_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1440_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1440_Task9" name="Route efficiency optimization (quarterly)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Route efficiency optimization (quarterly): In response to sustained fuel price increases: (a) Route Planners analyze delivery route efficiency: (i) average km per delivery, (ii) fuel consumption per delivery, (iii) load factor (kg delivered per liter of fuel), (iv) identify routes with below-average fuel efficiency, (b) optimization actions: (i) consolidate multi-stop routes to reduce total km, (ii) shift deliveries from low-efficiency to high-efficiency 3PL partners, (iii) evaluate DC-to-store direct routes vs. hub-and-spoke, (iv) consider intermodal options (RoRo ferry vs. truck-only for inter-island routes), (c) target: maintain or improve deliveries per liter of fuel despite fuel price increases
Responsible (R): Route Planners / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1440_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1440_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1440_Task10" name="Annual fuel cost budget planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual fuel cost budget planning: For annual freight budget preparation: (a) Finance Controller and Logistics Manager project next year&#x27;s fuel cost based on: (i) DOE fuel price forecasts, (ii) planned store expansion (10–15 new stores = new routes), (iii) route efficiency improvement targets, (iv) 3PL contract rate and surcharge terms, (b) present freight budget to CFO with fuel price sensitivity analysis (best case, base case, worst case)
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1440_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1440_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1440_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1440_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1440_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-258 (ensure controlled execution — Last-Mile &amp; Delivery Partners (PA-06.3).) | - operational: Logistics Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Logistics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1440_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1440_Annotation12" targetRef="W1440_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
