    <bpmn:process id="W_W1488" name="W1488. Customer Bulk Sand, Gravel &amp; Cement Delivery Scheduling, Weight Ticket Verification &amp; Site Unloading Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases bulk construction materials (sand, gravel, cement bags, fill soil, crushed stone) at store or via trade account; delivery required due to weight/volume
Frequency: ~15–30 bulk delivery requests per store per month; higher during dry season construction peak (Jan–May)
Volume: ~3,000–6,000 bulk deliveries/month chain-wide; average order: 2–5 cubic meters sand/gravel or 50–200 bags cement
Owner: Logistics Coordinator
Participants: Customer, Sales Associate, Logistics Coordinator, Delivery Driver, Third-Party Hauler (for oversized loads)
Source: workflow W1488 — Customer Bulk Sand, Gravel &amp; Cement Delivery Scheduling, Weight Ticket Verification &amp; Site Unloading Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1488_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1488_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1488_Lane2" name="Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1488_Lane3" name="Delivery Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1488_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1488_Start5" name="Customer purchases bulk construction materials (sand, gravel, cement bags, fill soil…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1488_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1488_Task6" name="Delivery order capture &amp; site assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Delivery order capture &amp; site assessment: At point of sale: (a) Sales Associate records delivery order: material type, volume/quantity, delivery address, site contact person and mobile number; (b) associate asks customer about site access: road width, overhead clearance, turning radius, ground firmness; (c) customer specifies preferred delivery date/time window; (d) if site is in a gated community or has restricted access hours: customer responsible for providing gate pass or access authorization; (e) order transmitted to Logistics Coordinator for scheduling
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1488_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1488_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1488_Task7" name="Delivery scheduling &amp; vehicle assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Delivery scheduling &amp; vehicle assignment: (a) Logistics Coordinator reviews delivery queue for the requested date; (b) assigns appropriate vehicle based on volume: (i) &lt; 2 cu.m.: 6-wheeler truck (max 6 cu.m.); (ii) 2–8 cu.m.: 10-wheeler truck (max 12 cu.m.); (iii) &gt; 8 cu.m.: split into multiple trips or assign 18-wheeler dump truck via third-party hauler; (c) if all BuildRight trucks committed: third-party hauler engaged per PA-06.3 rate card; (d) customer receives SMS confirmation with delivery date, time window (±2 hours), truck plate number, and driver contact; (e) delivery fee calculated by distance zone: Zone A (0–5 km): PHP 500; Zone B (5–15 km): PHP 1,000; Zone C (15–30 km): PHP 1,800; Zone D (&gt; 30 km): PHP 2,500+
Responsible (R): Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 10 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1488_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1488_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1488_Task8" name="Weight ticket verification at loading">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Weight ticket verification at loading: At DC or supplier yard: (a) truck drives onto certified weighbridge → tare weight recorded; (b) material loaded (by volume scoop for sand/gravel, by pallet for cement); (c) truck re-weighed → gross weight recorded; (d) net weight = gross − tare; (e) weight ticket printed with: material type, net weight, date, weighbridge certification number, driver signature; (f) if net weight is &lt; 95% of ordered volume-equivalent weight: additional material loaded; (g) weight ticket accompanies delivery as proof of quantity
Responsible (R): Delivery Driver / Weighbridge Operator
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 15–20 min per load</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1488_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1488_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1488_Task9" name="Site delivery &amp; unloading">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Site delivery &amp; unloading: At customer site: (a) driver calls site contact 30 minutes before arrival; (b) driver verifies site access per assessment in Step 1; (c) unloading method depends on material and site: (i) sand/gravel/soil: truck dumps material at designated spot on site (hydraulic lift); (ii) bagged cement: driver + 1 helper stack bags at designated area (max 200 bags manually; larger quantities require customer-provided labor or forklift); (d) customer/site representative signs delivery receipt acknowledging quantity and condition; (e) driver photographs delivered material as proof of placement; (f) any discrepancy or damage noted on delivery receipt before signing
Responsible (R): Delivery Driver
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 30–60 min per delivery (includes travel time from last delivery)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1488_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1488_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1488_Task10" name="Delivery confirmation &amp; weight ticket reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Delivery confirmation &amp; weight ticket reconciliation: (a) driver returns signed delivery receipt and weight ticket to Logistics Coordinator; (b) system matches delivery receipt to sales order; (c) weight ticket filed for DTI legal-metrology regime (per RA 7394/RA 9236) compliance; (d) if customer disputes quantity: weight ticket serves as primary evidence; (e) delivery status updated to &quot;Completed&quot; in system, triggering revenue recognition; (f) customer satisfaction SMS survey sent 24 hours post-delivery
Responsible (R): Delivery Driver / Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 5 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1488_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1488_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1488_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1488_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1488_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-258 (ensure controlled execution — Last-Mile &amp; Delivery Partners (PA-06.3).) | - operational: Logistics Coordinator review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Logistics Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1488_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1488_Annotation12" targetRef="W1488_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
